(vox-fuzz entry point.

 Subcommands:
   vox-fuzz version                          print the version, exit 0
   vox-fuzz gen [--seed N] [--count N]       generate, compile, and run
              [--budget N] [--timeout MS]    random Vox programs
              [--vox PATH] [--core DIR]
              [--out DIR] [--layout MODE]
   anything else                             usage to stderr, exit 2

 Flag precedence for --vox / --core is flag beats environment beats
 compiled-in default. runner.vox declares vox_binary / vox_core and then
 applies the VOX / VOX_CORE_PATH environment guards at load time, before
 this body runs; 'parse options' Sets them again afterwards, so an
 explicit flag always wins. See acceptance item 3.

 Written for vox 0.4.4. Bug #21 is fixed there - a string literal in an
 If condition inside a function body now resolves correctly - so the flag
 spellings are written inline as the English they are, not hoisted into
 top-level globals as the 0.4.2-era plan snippet had to. 'count' and
 'version' are free words on 0.4.4; 'flag', 'args', 'empty', 'ver' are
 still reserved, so no local here carries any of those names.)

see "./version.vox".
see "./rng.vox".
see "./gen_literals.vox".
see "./harness.vox".
see "./runner.vox".
see "./gen_core.vox".
see "./gen_buffers.vox".
see "./gen_files.vox".
see "./gen_collections.vox".
see "./gen_text.vox".
see "./gen_things.vox".
see "./gen_flow.vox".
see "./gen_misc.vox".
see "./findings.vox".
see "./loop_gen.vox".

(Defaults. Declared, not Set - language note 13.)
a number called opt_seed is 1.
a number called opt_count is 100.
a number called opt_budget is 12.
a number called opt_timeout is 10000.

(Usage goes to stderr (fd 2), not stdout, so a script that asks for help
 cannot mistake it for program output. Open the descriptor, write each
 line, close it.)

To 'print usage'.
    open a file for writing called 'the error stream' at 2.
    Write "usage: vox-fuzz <command> [options]\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Write "\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Write "commands:\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Write "  gen        generate, compile, and run random Vox programs\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Write "  version    print the version\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Write "\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Write "gen options:\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Write "  --seed N       first seed (default 1)\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Write "  --count N      how many programs (default 100)\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Write "  --budget N     statements per program (default 12)\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Write "  --timeout MILLISECONDS per-program time limit (default 10000)\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Write "  --vox PATH     vox binary (default ../vox/target/release/vox)\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Write "  --core DIR     coreasm dir (default ../vox/coreasm)\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Write "  --out DIR      findings directory (default ./findings)\n  --keep DIR     also save every generated program here (default: off)\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Write "  --layout MODE  random (default) or plain: whether a program's whitespace is drawn or laid out one statement per line\n" to 'the error stream'.
    Close 'the error stream'.

(A campaign that thinks it randomised its layout and did not is a
 campaign that proves less than its operator believes, and a typo in a
 flag value is the cheapest way to end up there - so an unrecognised
 --layout is a hard stop, not a silent fall back to plain.)

To 'set the layout mode' with a text called 'the requested mode'.
    If 'the requested mode' is "random" then,
        'gen set layout' of "random",
        Return a number, 0.
    If 'the requested mode' is "plain" then,
        'gen set layout' of "plain",
        Return a number, 0.
    open a file for writing called 'the layout error stream' at 2.
    Write "vox-fuzz: --layout takes 'random' or 'plain', not '{'the requested mode'}'.\n" to 'the layout error stream'.
    Close 'the layout error stream'.
    Exit 2.

(Parse the gen subcommand's flags. arguments's all is argv[1..], so
 element 1 is the subcommand itself and the flags start at element 2.

 Two shapes here are load-bearing - language note 6b. Every If sits at
 While level (none nests the increment), and the position increment is
 the loop's last plain statement, so its period closes the loop. An
 earlier draft nested the flag Ifs inside the value-position guard with
 the increment inside it, which both left the loop open - swallowing
 everything after it - and never advanced on an odd argument count,
 spinning forever on `vox-fuzz gen --seed` with no value.

 Bug #21 being fixed means the flag spellings compare inline; no hoisted
 globals. A flag given with no value reads its target from "" - `as a
 number` yields 0 - accepted for v1.)

To 'parse options'.
    a list called 'the given arguments' is arguments's all.
    a number called 'how many were given' is 'the given arguments's length.
    a number called 'the position' is 2.
    While 'the position' is less than or equal to 'how many were given',
        a text called 'the option' is element 'the position' of 'the given arguments',
        a number called 'the value position' is 'the position' add 1,
        a text called 'the value' is "",
        If 'the value position' is less than or equal to 'how many were given' then,
            Set 'the value' to element 'the value position' of 'the given arguments'.
        If 'the option' is "--seed" then,
            Set opt_seed to 'the value' as a number.
        If 'the option' is "--count" then,
            Set opt_count to 'the value' as a number.
        If 'the option' is "--budget" then,
            Set opt_budget to 'the value' as a number.
        If 'the option' is "--timeout" then,
            Set opt_timeout to 'the value' as a number.
        If 'the option' is "--vox" then,
            Set vox_binary to 'the value'.
        If 'the option' is "--core" then,
            Set vox_core to 'the value'.
        If 'the option' is "--out" then,
            Set findings_dir to 'the value'.
        If 'the option' is "--keep" then,
            Set keep_dir to 'the value'.
        If 'the option' is "--layout" then,
            'set the layout mode' of 'the value'.
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 2.

(Dispatch. Top-level literal comparisons are legal - bug #21 bites only
 inside function bodies.)

a list called 'the command arguments' is arguments's all.
a number called 'the command argument tally' is 'the command arguments's length.
If 'the command argument tally' is 0 then,
    'print usage',
    Exit 2.

a text called 'the command' is element 1 of 'the command arguments'.
If 'the command' is equal to "version" then,
    'fuzz version',
    Exit 0.

If 'the command' is equal to "gen" then,
    'parse options',
    Print "vox-fuzz gen: seeds {opt_seed}.. count {opt_count} budget {opt_budget} timeout {opt_timeout}ms",
    'fuzz gen run' of opt_seed and opt_count and opt_budget and opt_timeout,
    Exit 0.

'print usage'.
Exit 2.